window.V.data.characters=[{id:"mash",name:"Mash Burnedead",kind:"Easton student",role:"Adler House first-year with no magic",rank:"student",side:"Mash's side",orgs:["h-easton","h-adler"],parents:["innocent-zero"],marks:0,status:"Active",arc:"s1",first:"Season 1, episode 1",featured:true,color:"#f3d38a",markNote:"Mash was born without magic, so he has no magic mark at all. The mark on his face is a fake that he paints on to pass as a mage. In a world where magic decides everything, that alone marks him for elimination.",bio:"A boy born without magic in a world where everyone has it. Raised in secret in the forest by Regro Burnedead, he trained his body until his muscles could do what spells do. When he is discovered, he enrols at Easton Magic Academy and aims to become a Divine Visionary so that he and his father can live in peace. At the end of the selection exam arc he learns that Innocent Zero is his biological father, who wants his heart. He loves cream puffs.",bioM:"In the manga Mash goes on to the Tri-Magic-Athalon and then faces his elder brothers and Innocent Zero himself in the final battle.",abilities:[{n:"Superhuman strength",d:"Breaks spells, walls and wands with his bare hands."},{n:"Speed and reflexes",d:"Fast enough to keep up with mages flying on brooms."},{n:"Endurance",d:"Shrugs off attacks that would put a trained mage down."}]},{id:"finn",name:"Finn Ames",kind:"Easton student",role:"Mash's roommate in Adler House",rank:"student",side:"Mash's side",orgs:["h-easton","h-adler"],status:"Active",arc:"s1",first:"Season 1, episode 2",featured:true,color:"#9fd0ff",bio:"Mash's first friend and roommate at Easton. Timid and kind, he lives in the shadow of his elder brother Rayne, but he stands by Mash and grows braver. During the selection exam he refuses to give in to Carpaccio, who admits that Finn's will is stronger than his own."},{id:"lance",name:"Lance Crown",kind:"Easton student",role:"Adler House gravity mage",rank:"student",side:"Mash's side",orgs:["h-easton","h-adler"],marks:2,status:"Active",arc:"s1",first:"Season 1",featured:true,color:"#c9a3ff",markNote:"A double-liner from the start: two lines, a rare sign of strong magic.",bio:"A gifted, cool-headed double-liner who fights with gravity magic. He wants to become a Divine Visionary to save his younger sister Anna, and is devoted to her. After duelling Mash he becomes his rival and friend. He defeats Wirth Madl of Magia Lupus and, during Innocent Zero's attack, the Criminal Cane Sitter Baby."},{id:"dot",name:"Dot Barrett",kind:"Easton student",role:"Adler House explosion mage",rank:"student",side:"Mash's side",orgs:["h-easton","h-adler"],status:"Active",arc:"s1",first:"Season 1",featured:true,color:"#ff8a65",bio:"A loud, hot-blooded Adler student who uses explosion magic and is jealous of anyone more popular with girls. He calls himself Mash's rival and becomes one of his closest friends. Against Magia Lupus he unlocks the cross on his forehead, which boosts his magic.",abilities:[{n:"Ira Kreuz",d:"The cross on his forehead that raises his magic power when he is pushed."}]},{id:"lemon",name:"Lemon Irvine",kind:"Easton student",role:"Adler House first-year",rank:"student",side:"Mash's side",orgs:["h-easton","h-adler"],status:"Active",arc:"s1",first:"Season 1, episode 2",featured:true,color:"#fff176",bio:"A first-year whom Mash saves on the day of the entrance exam. She declares herself his fiancée from then on. Her magic summons binding tools such as cuffs and chains."},{id:"tom",name:"Tom Knowles",kind:"Easton student",role:"Adler senior on the Duelo team",rank:"student",side:"Mash's side",orgs:["h-easton","h-adler"],status:"Active",arc:"s1",first:"Season 1, episode 3",color:"#a5d6a7",bio:"An Adler senior on the Duelo team who recruits Mash after seeing what he can do."},{id:"max",name:"Max Land",kind:"Easton student",role:"Adler senior and Divine Visionary candidate",rank:"student",side:"Mash's side",orgs:["h-easton","h-adler"],status:"Active",arc:"exam",first:"Season 2",color:"#ffcc80",bio:"An Adler senior who enters the Divine Visionary Selection Exam to protect the younger students. His magic changes the size of objects. In the first stage he teams up with Mash."},{id:"silva",name:"Silva Arm",kind:"Easton student",role:"Iron mage who challenges Mash",rank:"student",side:"Mash's side",orgs:["h-easton"],status:"Active",arc:"s1",first:"Season 1, episode 5",color:"#b0bec5",canon:"check",bio:"A student with iron magic who beats Dot and makes Mash drop his cream puff in a forest class. Mash takes up his challenge and beats him. Later Mash frees him after Abel turns students into dolls."},{id:"abel",name:"Abel Walker",kind:"Easton student",role:"Lang prefect and leader of Magia Lupus",rank:"student",side:"Antagonist",orgs:["h-easton","h-lang","h-magia-lupus"],status:"Active",arc:"lupus",first:"Season 1",featured:true,color:"#9575cd",bio:"The prefect of Lang House and leader of Magia Lupus, who believes people should be ranked by their talent. His magic turns people into puppets and dolls, a belief shaped by his mother's murder. Mash defeats him, and Abel frees the students he turned into dolls. Innocent Zero then sends Cell War to kill him."},{id:"abyss",name:"Abyss Razor",kind:"Easton student",role:"Second Fang of Magia Lupus",rank:"student",side:"Mash's side",orgs:["h-easton","h-lang","h-magia-lupus"],status:"Active",arc:"lupus",first:"Season 1",color:"#7e57c2",bio:"Abel's best friend and the Second Fang of Magia Lupus. Born with the Evil Eye, he was feared and shunned for it. After Mash defeats him and treats him as a person, he comes over to Mash's side."},{id:"wirth",name:"Wirth Madl",kind:"Easton student",role:"Third Fang of Magia Lupus",rank:"student",side:"Antagonist",orgs:["h-easton","h-lang","h-magia-lupus"],status:"Active",arc:"lupus",first:"Season 1",color:"#8d6e63",bio:"The Third Fang of Magia Lupus and Orter Madl's younger brother. He fights with mud magic. Lance defeats him during the raid on the Lang dormitory."},{id:"love",name:"Love Cute",kind:"Easton student",role:"Fifth Fang of Magia Lupus",rank:"student",side:"Antagonist",orgs:["h-easton","h-lang","h-magia-lupus"],status:"Active",arc:"lupus",first:"Season 1",color:"#f06292",bio:"The Fifth Fang of Magia Lupus, who summons tornadoes. She faces Dot during the raid on Lang."},{id:"olore",name:"Olore Andrew",kind:"Easton student",role:"Sixth Fang of Magia Lupus",rank:"student",side:"Antagonist",orgs:["h-easton","h-lang","h-magia-lupus"],status:"Active",arc:"lupus",first:"Season 1, episode 7",color:"#4fc3f7",bio:"The Sixth Fang of Magia Lupus. He creates an underwater space and turns into a shark to fight in it. Mash defeats him underwater."},{id:"margarette",name:"Margarette Macaron",kind:"Easton student",role:"Prefect of Orca House",rank:"student",side:"Mash's side",orgs:["h-easton","h-orca"],marks:2,status:"Active",arc:"exam",first:"Season 2, episode 14",color:"#f48fb1",markNote:"A double-liner. Margarette's two marks are musical: a treble clef on one side of the face and a note under the other eye.",bio:"The prefect of Orca House, a double-liner who fights with sound magic. Orter Madl sends Margarette to stop Mash from reaching the exam, but Rayne Ames intervenes. In the third stage of the selection exam Margarette duels Mash and loses."},{id:"carpaccio",name:"Carpaccio Luo-Yang",kind:"Easton student",role:"Orca first-year with a Master Cane",rank:"student",side:"Antagonist",orgs:["h-easton","h-orca"],status:"Active",arc:"exam",first:"Season 2, episode 17",color:"#80cbc4",bio:"An Orca first-year chosen by a Master Cane. He cannot feel pain: damage is absorbed by a goddess statue and passed on to his enemies. He captures and wounds Finn in the exam until Mash shatters the statue and defeats him."},{id:"rayne",name:"Rayne Ames",kind:"Divine Visionary",role:"Holder of the Sword Cane, Adler prefect",rank:"dv",side:"Magic Bureau",cane:"Sword Cane",orgs:["h-visionaries","h-easton","h-adler"],marks:2,status:"Active",arc:"s1",first:"Season 1",featured:true,color:"#90caf9",markNote:"Two lines under his eyes. A third line appears when he fights seriously, which makes him the youngest mage to reach three lines.",bio:"Finn's elder brother, the prefect of Adler House and the youngest of the Divine Visionaries, holder of the Sword Cane. He creates and controls swords. Cold on the surface, he helps Mash reach Abel, comes to respect him and defends him from Margarette."},{id:"orter",name:"Orter Madl",kind:"Divine Visionary",role:"Holder of the Desert Cane",rank:"dv",side:"Magic Bureau",cane:"Desert Cane",orgs:["h-visionaries"],status:"Active",arc:"exam",first:"Season 2",color:"#e0b26b",bio:"A strict Divine Visionary who holds the Desert Cane, fights with sand and heads the Magical Power Administration. He believes in the order of the magic world, wants Mash removed and sends Margarette after him. He is Wirth Madl's elder brother."},{id:"ryoh",name:"Ryoh Grantz",kind:"Divine Visionary",role:"Holder of the Light Cane",rank:"dv",side:"Magic Bureau",cane:"Light Cane",orgs:["h-visionaries"],status:"Active",arc:"exam",first:"Season 2",color:"#fff6c2",bio:"The Divine Visionary who holds the Light Cane and captains the Magic Security Forces. His light beams can cut through almost anything. He is one of the Visionaries who side with Mash.",bioM:"In the manga he saves Domina after Domina sacrifices himself for Mash."},{id:"kaldo",name:"Kaldo Gehenna",kind:"Divine Visionary",role:"Holder of the Flame Cane",rank:"dv",side:"Magic Bureau",cane:"Flame Cane",orgs:["h-visionaries"],status:"Active",arc:"exam",first:"Season 2",color:"#ff7043",bio:"The Divine Visionary who holds the Flame Cane and heads the Magic Talent Administration. His fire magic includes a sword of black flame. He tests Mash with a deadly pointing game that ends in a draw."},{id:"agito",name:"Agito Tyrone",kind:"Divine Visionary",role:"Holder of the Dragon Cane",rank:"dv",side:"Magic Bureau",cane:"Dragon Cane",orgs:["h-visionaries"],status:"Active",arc:"exam",first:"Season 2",color:"#81c784",bio:"The Divine Visionary who holds the Dragon Cane and heads the Magical Creatures Administration. He fights through his pet dragon, which he can turn into a much larger form."},{id:"tsurara",name:"Tsurara Halestone",kind:"Divine Visionary",role:"Holder of the Ice Cane",rank:"dv",side:"Magic Bureau",cane:"Ice Cane",orgs:["h-visionaries"],status:"Active",arc:"exam",first:"Season 2",color:"#b3e5fc",bio:"The Divine Visionary who holds the Ice Cane and heads the Magic Research Administration. Her magic can freeze anything."},{id:"renatus",name:"Renatus Revol",kind:"Divine Visionary",role:"Holder of the Immortal Cane",rank:"dv",side:"Magic Bureau",cane:"Immortal Cane",orgs:["h-visionaries"],status:"Active",arc:"exam",first:"Season 2",color:"#ce93d8",bio:"The Divine Visionary who holds the Immortal Cane and heads the Magical Cemetery Administration. He summons the body parts of the undead and is himself immortal."},{id:"sophina",name:"Sophina Biblia",kind:"Divine Visionary",role:"Holder of the Knowledge Cane",rank:"dv",side:"Magic Bureau",cane:"Knowledge Cane",orgs:["h-visionaries"],status:"Active",arc:"exam",first:"Season 2",color:"#a1887f",bio:"The Divine Visionary who holds the Knowledge Cane and heads the Forbidden Magical Texts Administration. Her magic controls words, and through them what her targets do."},{id:"wahlberg",name:"Wahlberg Baigan",kind:"Headmaster",role:"Headmaster of Easton",rank:"faculty",rankNote:"A former Divine Visionary.",side:"Mash's side",orgs:["h-easton"],marks:3,status:"Active",arc:"s1",first:"Season 1, episode 1",featured:true,color:"#d1c4e9",markNote:"A three-line mage, one of the very few in history. He explains the gulf between two-line and three-line mages during the selection exam arc.",bio:"Easton's headmaster, a former Divine Visionary and one of the very few mages with three magic-mark lines. His magic controls space. He sees something in Mash and protects him. When Innocent Zero attacks the exam he fights him and the body of his own teacher, Adam Jobs."},{id:"adam",name:"Adam Jobs",kind:"Mage",role:"Founder of the Bureau of Magic and Wahlberg's teacher",side:"Civilian",status:"Deceased",arc:"attack",first:"Season 2, episode 21",color:"#90a4ae",canon:"check",bio:"The great mage who taught Wahlberg, founded the Bureau of Magic and designed the Divine Visionary system. His magic of darkness erases its target. Innocent Zero brings back his body during the attack on Easton, and Wahlberg defeats it."},{id:"innocent-zero",name:"Innocent Zero",kind:"Mage",role:"Mash's biological father",side:"Antagonist",orgs:["h-zero-family"],status:"Active",arc:"attack",first:"Season 2",featured:true,color:"#ef5350",bio:"The most dangerous mage of the age, a former pupil of Adam Jobs who seeks immortality. He fathered six sons, Mash the youngest, and plans to take their hearts. He can change his appearance and controls time: he freezes the exam audience, ages half of Wahlberg's body and turns back time to undo Wahlberg's spell, until Mash kicks him in the face.",bioM:"In the manga he leads his remaining sons against the magic world and is the final enemy Mash has to beat."},{id:"cell",name:"Cell War",kind:"Mage",role:"Innocent Zero's clone mage",side:"Antagonist",status:"Defeated",arc:"lupus",first:"Season 1, episode 12",color:"#e1bee7",bio:"A clone created to serve Innocent Zero, with carbon and diamond magic. He comes to Easton to kill Abel; when Mash smashes his magic mirror, the school learns Mash has only ever used his muscles. He returns during the exam, and Mash defeats him again. He reveals Innocent Zero's plan to harvest his sons' hearts."},{id:"sitter-baby",name:"Sitter Baby",kind:"Criminal Cane",role:"Criminal Cane under Innocent Zero",side:"Antagonist",orgs:["h-criminal-canes"],status:"Defeated",arc:"attack",first:"Season 2, episode 20",color:"#ffab91",bio:"One of the Criminal Canes, former death-row prisoners working for Innocent Zero. Sitter Baby's magic turns people, or the user, into babies. Lance defeats Sitter Baby during the attack on the exam."},{id:"doom",name:"Doom",kind:"Mage",role:"Innocent Zero's eldest son",sp:"m",side:"Antagonist",orgs:["h-zero-family"],parents:["innocent-zero"],status:"Active",arc:"final",first:"Manga",color:"#b71c1c",bio:"Innocent Zero's eldest son and the strongest of Mash's brothers. He wields the Master Cane Caladbolg and uses mirror magic that copies movements and makes duplicates."},{id:"famin",name:"Famin",kind:"Mage",role:"Innocent Zero's second son",sp:"m",side:"Antagonist",orgs:["h-zero-family"],parents:["innocent-zero"],status:"Active",arc:"final",first:"Manga",color:"#c62828",bio:"Innocent Zero's second son. He makes things invisible and attacks with playing cards that serve as his wand."},{id:"epidem",name:"Epidem",kind:"Mage",role:"Innocent Zero's third son",sp:"m",side:"Antagonist",orgs:["h-zero-family"],parents:["innocent-zero"],status:"Defeated",arc:"final",first:"Manga",color:"#d84315",bio:"Innocent Zero's third son, who creates and controls orichalcum. Lance and Dot defeat him together."},{id:"delisaster",name:"Delisaster",kind:"Mage",role:"Innocent Zero's fourth son",sp:"m",side:"Antagonist",orgs:["h-zero-family"],parents:["innocent-zero"],status:"Active",arc:"final",first:"Manga",color:"#e53935",bio:"Innocent Zero's fourth son, who creates and controls guandao polearms."},{id:"domina",name:"Domina Blowelive",kind:"Walkis student",role:"Innocent Zero's fifth son",sp:"m",side:"Mash's side",orgs:["h-zero-family","h-walkis"],parents:["innocent-zero"],status:"Active",arc:"tma",first:"Manga",color:"#4dd0e1",canon:"check",bio:"The top student of Walkis Magic Academy and Innocent Zero's fifth son, who fights with water magic. He meets Mash in the Tri-Magic-Athalon, later sides with him and sacrifices himself for Mash; Ryoh Grantz saves him. The romanisation of his family name varies between sources."},{id:"levis",name:"Lévis Rosequartz",kind:"Walkis student",role:"Walkis student, son of the Bureau chief",sp:"m",side:"Antagonist",orgs:["h-walkis"],status:"Active",arc:"tma",first:"Manga",color:"#ffd54f",bio:"A Walkis student and the son of the head of the Bureau of Magic. He wears an eyepatch and controls magnetism and electricity."},{id:"regro",name:"Regro Burnedead",kind:"Civilian",role:"Mash's adoptive father",side:"Civilian",marks:1,status:"Active",arc:"pre",first:"Season 1, episode 1",color:"#bcaaa4",markNote:"An ordinary single-liner, like most mages.",bio:"The old man who found the infant Mash in the forest and raised him in secret, knowing a child without magic would be eliminated. Mash fights to become a Divine Visionary so they can live in peace."},{id:"brad",name:"Brad Coleman",kind:"Civilian",role:"Police officer who discovers Mash",side:"Civilian",status:"Active",arc:"s1",first:"Season 1, episode 1",color:"#a1887f",bio:"A corrupt police officer who finds out that Mash has no magic. He ends up helping Mash enrol at Easton."},{id:"anna",name:"Anna Crown",kind:"Civilian",role:"Lance's younger sister",side:"Civilian",status:"Active",arc:"s1",first:"Season 1",color:"#f8bbd0",bio:"Lance's beloved younger sister, who suffers from an illness that eats away at her magic and her life. Saving her is why Lance wants to become a Divine Visionary."}];
